From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: fix the sub2video perf regressions
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0058-fix-the-sub2video-perf-regressions.patch

ffmpeg sends a subtitle picture to the filter graph when the graph asks
for one, not again with every video frame: burning picture subtitles in
doesn't scale and upload the same picture frame after frame.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
@@ -2934,7 +2934,8 @@ static void sub2video_heartbeat(InputFil
            or if we need to initialize the system, update the
            overlaid subpicture and its start/end times */
         sub2video_update(ifp, pts2 + 1, NULL);
-    else
+
+    if (av_buffersrc_get_nb_failed_requests(ifp->ifilter.filter))
         sub2video_push_ref(ifp, pts2);
 }
 
